<RSLogix5000Content SchemaRevision="1.0" SoftwareRevision="16.03" TargetType="AddOnInstructionDefinition" ContainsContext="true" Owner="Dale Reed, Rockwell Automation" ExportDate="Fri Jul 31 11:00:04 2009" ExportOptions="References Context">
<Controller Use="Context" Name="ProcessObjix">
<DataTypes Use="Context">
</DataTypes>
<AddOnInstructionDefinitions Use="Context">
<AddOnInstructionDefinition Use="Target" Name="L_SUB" Revision="1.0" RevisionExtension="00 Release" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" ExecutePrescan="false" ExecutePostscan="false" ExecuteEnableInFalse="false" CreatedDate="2008-12-10T21:30:18.915Z" CreatedBy="Not Available" EditedDate="2009-07-31T14:59:51.822Z"
 EditedBy="Not Available" SoftwareRevision="v16.03">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Subtract (64-bit)]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[Initial Release]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[Subtracts two LINT (signed 64-bit) values and returns a LINT (signed 64-bit) difference.
Also provides math status bits for Carry (borrow), Negative, Overflow and Zero result
(equivalent to built-in S:C, S:N, S:V, S:Z).]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
<Parameter Name="Inp_A" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[First Input, 64-bit Integer]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Inp_B" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Second Input, 64-bit Integer]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Out" DataType="LINT" Usage="InOut" Radix="Decimal" Required="true" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Difference, 64-bit Integer]]>
</Description>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_C" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Carry (borrow!) result]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_N" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Negative result]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_V" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Overflow result]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
<Parameter Name="Sts_Z" DataType="BOOL" Usage="Output" Radix="Decimal" Required="false" Visible="true">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Zero result]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00</DefaultData>
</Parameter>
</Parameters>
<LocalTags>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Diff" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="3" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[20- and 24-bit fields of Out (difference)]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_B" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="3" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[20- and 24-bit fields of Inp_B]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_A" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="3" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[20- and 24-bit fields of Inp_A]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_Out" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="2" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Output as two 32-bit DINTs]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_InpB" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="2" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Input B as two 32-bit DINTs]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
<LocalTag Name="Wrk_InpA" DataType="DINT" Dimensions="2" Radix="Decimal">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Input A as two 32-bit DINTs]]>
</Description>
<DefaultData>00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00</DefaultData>
</LocalTag>
</LocalTags>
<Routines>
<Routine Name="Logic" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Do 64-bit subtraction]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
L_SUB : Subtract (64-bit)
============================================================
Revision 1.0-00 Release:  2009-Jun-31
Initial Release
============================================================
Subtracts two LINT (signed 64-bit) values and returns a LINT (signed 64-bit) difference.
Also provides math status bits for Carry (borrow), Negative, Overflow and Zero result
(equivalent to built-in S:C, S:N, S:V, S:Z).

This instruction breaks the LINT addends into three DINTs
(24 bits, 20 bits and 20 bits) to do the math in order to
avoid generating a Controller MINOR FAULT on overflow.
(Sample code provided in RSLogix 5000 Online Help is much
smaller and faster, but causes numerous Minor Faults on
Overflows -- S:V -- on the low-order difference!  The controller must
take time to log the minor faults, and many users do not want to see
Minor Faults on normal math operations.  See the RSLogix 5000
Help Topic "Arithmetic Status Flags" for more information.)
===================================================
CONVERT LINTs TO DINTs
===================================================
These COPies take the input LINTs and break them into pairs of DINTs so we can do math on them.
Logix V17 has a LINT data type, but math instructions (and AOI Input and Output Parameters) don't support LINT.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Inp_A,Wrk_InpA[0],2)COP(Inp_B,Wrk_InpB[0],2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
SPREAD 64 BITS ACROSS THREE DINTs
===================================================
If we do the math on 32-bit DINTs, the math on the low-order DINT (bits .0 to .31 of the 64-bit value)
will cause Overflows, setting the S:V status bit and THROWING A MINOR FAULT.

To avoid the Minor Fault, we take the two DINTs and break them up into THREE:
a 24 bit low-order DINT,
a 20-bit middle DINT, and
a 20-bit high-order DINT.

Doing the math on less than 30 bits per ADD ensures we never have an Overflow that throws a Minor Fault.
The BTDs split the 64 bits of Input A among the three DINTs used in the math.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[FLL(0,Wrk_A[0],3)BTD(Wrk_InpA[0],0,Wrk_A[0],0,24)BTD(Wrk_InpA[0],24,Wrk_A[1],0,8)BTD(Wrk_InpA[1],0,Wrk_A[1],8,12)BTD(Wrk_InpA[1],12,Wrk_A[2],0,20);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This rung does the same for Input B:  two 32-bit DINTs are split into a 24-bit and two 20-bit DINTs.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[FLL(0,Wrk_B[0],3)BTD(Wrk_InpB[0],0,Wrk_B[0],0,24)BTD(Wrk_InpB[0],24,Wrk_B[1],0,8)BTD(Wrk_InpB[1],0,Wrk_B[1],8,12)BTD(Wrk_InpB[1],12,Wrk_B[2],0,20);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
DIFFERENCE, WITH BORROW
===================================================
Now do the actual subtraction.  Any Carry (really, BORROW) bits will be in bit 24
of the low-order difference, or bit 20 of the middle or high-order difference.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SUB(Wrk_A[0],Wrk_B[0],Wrk_Diff[0])SUB(Wrk_A[1],Wrk_B[1],Wrk_Diff[1])SUB(Wrk_A[2],Wrk_B[2],Wrk_Diff[2]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the low-order sum had a borrow, subtract 1 from the middle difference.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Diff[0].24)SUB(Wrk_Diff[1],1,Wrk_Diff[1]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the middle difference had a borrow, subtract 1 from the high-order difference.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Diff[1].20)SUB(Wrk_Diff[2],1,Wrk_Diff[2]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
GATHER 64-BIT RESULT FROM THREE DINTs
===================================================
Finally, take the 20-, 20- and 24-bit results and put them into 2 32-bit DINT output words.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[BTD(Wrk_Diff[0],0,Wrk_Out[0],0,24)BTD(Wrk_Diff[1],0,Wrk_Out[0],24,8)BTD(Wrk_Diff[1],8,Wrk_Out[1],0,12)BTD(Wrk_Diff[2],0,Wrk_Out[1],12,20);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
INSTRUCTION STATUS BITS
===================================================

These four rungs generate the result STATUS bits, just like S:C, S:N, S:V and S:Z
are generated by built-in math instructions.

The difference is that our Sts_V doesn't throw a Minor Fault.  So you'll need to
deal with Sts_V in the code that uses this AOI....

If the high-order difference generated a Carry, set Sts_C.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Diff[2].20)OTE(Sts_C);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If the highest bit (.19) of the high-order difference is set, the result is NEGATIVE.
After all, we're doing a LINT (signed 64-bit integer) , not a ULINT (unsigned 64-bit integer)!]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Wrk_Out[1].31)OTE(Sts_N);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If both inputs are positive and the result is negative, or if both inputs are
negative and the result is positive, we had an OVERFLOW: set Sts_V.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(Wrk_InpA[1].31) XIO(Wrk_InpB[1].31) XIO(Wrk_Out[1].31) ,XIO(Wrk_InpA[1].31) XIC(Wrk_InpB[1].31) XIC(Wrk_Out[1].31) ]OTE(Sts_V);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[If both resulting DINTs are zero, the LINT is zero.  Set Sts_Z if the result is ZERO.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(Wrk_Out[1],0)EQU(Wrk_Out[0],0)OTE(Sts_Z);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[===================================================
CONVERT DINTs TO LINT
===================================================
The two 32-bit DINT outputs are converted back to a LINT, the actual output of the instruction.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[COP(Wrk_Out[0],Out,1);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</AddOnInstructionDefinition>
</AddOnInstructionDefinitions>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
